name=Cookie Slicer
id=CookieSlicer
description=Cookie Cheetah's own performance mod (AKA). The Cookie Slicer button on the main menu (top right) and the F8 key in game (Options > Mods to change) open a big black / mint window (Thai / English) with three pages. Performance: your PC now (FPS, game RAM, PC RAM, CPU, game main thread; point at a number to see what it means and how yours looks), what the chosen settings should save (about), FPS measured before / after a change, and the settings: levels Undo all / Balanced / Smooth / Max plus one switch per setting (the game's own options that cost CPU / RAM for little you can see: unseen zombies update less, plain zombie clothes, no blood on weapons, windows drawn 30 times a second, lighting 15 per second, at most 10 ragdolls; weak PC after a restart: compressed textures, textures up to 1024, no corpse shadows). Shader: with the Cookie Slicer Helper v1.1.0, a real screen shader drawn after the game's own one (media/shaders/cookie_post.*): 8 styles (Natural, Golden Hour, True Film, Night Glow, Vivid, Cinema, Retro, Intense Dark) with sliders (strength, brightness, contrast, colour, warm / cool, glow, dark edges, sharpness, grain), a check whether this PC can run it (helper, graphics card, OpenGL, measured ms per frame), quality Auto / Low / Medium / High, "Fit my PC", and a before / after line on the live game; about 11 MB of graphics memory at 1080p, no PC RAM. Without the helper: basic looks (Natural, Cinema, Retro, Intense Dark) and brightness, no FPS cost. Version Slicer: mod and helper versions, game RAM, how to install / update / remove the helper. Map loading: the work every mod does for each map square that loads runs a little at a time over the next frames, and work only the server needs is skipped in players' games (Cookie Square Queue). Cookie Profiler measures each mod's Lua time when Zomboid/Lua/CookieProfile_client.txt or CookieProfile_server.txt exists. Optional Cookie Slicer Helper (installed outside the game) adds CPU / RAM numbers and more RAM for the game. Keep it at the top of the mod list.
